DayWeave is an independently implemented MIT-licensed application.

It uses OR-Tools (Apache-2.0), FastAPI (MIT), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause),
icalendar (BSD-2-Clause), and recurring-ical-events (LGPL-3.0-or-later)
as separately installed, unmodified Python dependencies. Their licenses
remain applicable to those dependencies. No dependency source is vendored.

Optional model capture uses separately obtained Qwen weights (Apache-2.0)
through Transformers (Apache-2.0) and PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause).
No model weights, private agent code, private source data, or server
credentials are included in the repository or release packages.
